      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The use of naval positioning and deliberate proximity to disputed reefs as a form of psychological signaling is a timeless aspect of maritime power dynamics. This \"sparse agitation\" approach, where one party demonstrates its presence without making a direct aggressive move, can effectively convey intent and demonstrate strength without escalating the situation. While technology has introduced new variables to the mix, such as the ability to detect and respond more quickly, the underlying psychology of signaling through symbols of naval presence remains a critical component of these power struggles.",
      "source": "target",
